Sightseeing ideas and planned routes
Here’s a simple 3-day plan you could use, based on a central Berlin emphasis. It’s flexible for pace and interests, and I can tailor it or add guided tours if you’d like.

Day 1 – Mitte highlights (great for a first-day city feel)
- Morning: TV Tower visit (Fernsehturm) and Alexanderplatz area
- Late morning/afternoon: Walk to Museum Island or the Berlin Cathedral (Berliner Dom)
- Afternoon stroll along Unter den Linden toward Brandenburg Gate
- Evening: Dinner around the historic Nikolaiviertel or nearby Hackescher Markt

Day 2 – Historic core and memorials
- Morning: Brandenburg Gate and the Reichstag Building (consider a tour of the Reichstag dome)
- Midday: Holocaust Memorial (Memorial to the Murdered Jews of Europe)
- Afternoon: Tiergarten stroll; Checkpoint Charlie and the Topography of Terror (if interested)
- Evening: Potsdamer Platz area for nightlife or a relaxed dinner

Day 3 – East Berlin and modern highlights
- Morning: East Side Gallery (open-air mural section of the Berlin Wall)
- Afternoon: Oberbaum Bridge area and continuing to nearby neighborhoods (Kreuzberg and Friedrichshain have good cafés and street art)
- Optional: Museum Island museum visits if you didn’t do them Day 1 or want more culture
- Evening: River Spree area or a relaxed final dinner in a local restaurant

